# Scheduled jobs for the self-hosted deployment.
#
# These are the same eight jobs, on the same schedules, that apps/web/vercel.json
# registers for the hosted deployment. Kept deliberately in lockstep: if the two
# drift, a self-hoster gets a quietly different product from the one documented,
# which is worse than having no scheduler at all. Change one, change the other.
#
# Every route authenticates with the `x-cron-secret` header and refuses the
# request when CRON_SECRET is unset, so this file does nothing useful until that
# variable is set in docker/.env. That is deliberate: an unauthenticated
# scheduler endpoint on a self-hosted box is a worse failure than no schedule.
#
# `-fsS` so curl stays quiet on success but still reports a real failure to the
# container log, and `--max-time` so a hung request cannot overlap the next tick.

*/15 * * * *  altorank-cron publish
*/10 * * * *  altorank-cron analyze
0 3 * * *     altorank-cron serp
0 4 * * *     altorank-cron analytics
0 5 * * *     altorank-cron exchange
0 7 * * *     altorank-cron generate
0 8 * * 1     altorank-cron geo
0 6 1 * *     altorank-cron reports
